{"body":"Part of #137. Triggered on 2026-11-10: the product owner's \\\"Send me a test\\\" (#136) said \\\"Test sent\\\", but no email arrived. Production D1 \\`email_message\\` and \\`test_invitation_index\\` are empty (no email was ever accepted by Cloudflare from the app), while a direct \\`cf email-sending send\\` from \\`team@notify.surveybeat.app\\` is accepted. The reason is stored only in the Organization Durable Object's send states, which nobody can see.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- After \"Send me a test\", the Pulse editor shows the test send's live state (queued, sending, sent, failed with the reason code such as \\`E_SENDER_NOT_VERIFIED\\` or \\`unknown\\`), refreshing until it settles.\n- Organization admins get a \"Failed emails\" list in Organization settings: the last 50 failed sends of any kind (kind, recipient, reason code, time), never any email body or token. Endpoint classified in \\`PrivacyRegistry.ts\\`.\n- If the email queue consumer itself errors before reaching the send store (so no state changes), that is visible too: the send stays \"queued\" past a threshold and the UI says so.\n- English and German copy; tests for each state.","comments":[],"title":"Show email send outcomes: test-send status and a failed-emails view"}

